// Auto-generated from legacy HTML by scripts/extract-pages.py
export const title = "Ganz Cortrol Integration Guide";
export const html = "<h1>Ganz Cortrol Integration Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<h2>1. Introduction</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.1 Prerequisites</h3>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>AIBridge FW version 10124 or greater.</li>\n<li>Ganz Cortrol Premier / Global VMS version 1.22 or greater.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.2 Understanding the Integration Architecture</h3>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 300\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"24\">&#128247;</text>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"24\">&#128247;</text>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"215\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"215\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <text x=\"90\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <rect x=\"330\" y=\"20\" width=\"170\" height=\"80\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f2f3f6\" stroke=\"#9aa0ac\"/>\n  <text x=\"415\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\" font-weight=\"700\">Ganz Cortrol VMS</text>\n  <rect x=\"360\" y=\"190\" width=\"130\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#0b0f19\"/>\n  <text x=\"425\" y=\"225\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\">AI Bridge</text>\n  <line x1=\"500\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"590\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\" marker-end=\"url(#arrg)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"590\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\" marker-end=\"url(#arrg)\"/>\n  <text x=\"600\" y=\"35\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">Object Metadata Display<tspan x=\"600\" dy=\"13\">Event Notification</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"600\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#e0a94c\">External Service (HTTP API)<tspan x=\"600\" dy=\"13\">AI Metadata &amp; Event</tspan></text>\n  <line x1=\"415\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"425\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrg\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f9c\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>IP cameras stream to both Cortrol VMS and AIBridge. AIBridge analyzes the stream through its AI apps and sends metadata and events to Cortrol VMS, and responds to Cortrol's search requests.</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<h2>2. Configuration</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.1 AIBridge Configuration</h3>\n<p>Add an AI app setting. Choose the app you want from Explore AI Apps.</p>\n<p>This guide uses LPR as an example, but an action handler can be registered for any of the 50+ apps AI Bridge supports.</p>\n<p>Click <strong>Add Rule</strong>, then add an event setting and the AI app's zone or detailed settings, then add an action setting.</p>\n\n<p>Select the Cortrol plugin, then click <strong>Add Cortrol Plugin Action</strong>, then click <strong>Edit</strong>.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:460px;\">\n<div class=\"modal-mock\">\n  <div class=\"modal-head\">Cortrol Plugin</div>\n  <div class=\"modal-body\">\n    <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:130px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n      <span>Server Address</span><input value=\"192.168.101.10\" disabled>\n      <span>Port</span><input value=\"443\" disabled>\n      <span>Username</span><input disabled>\n      <span>Password</span><input disabled>\n      <span>Use Recording Server</span><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled style=\"width:auto;\">\n      <span>Metadata Enable</span><input type=\"checkbox\" checked disabled style=\"width:auto;\">\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"modal-foot\"><span class=\"btn small\">Cancel</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Login</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Apply</span></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Enter the Cortrol VMS server address, port, username, and password, then use Login to verify the connection</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\"><strong>Note.</strong> When Metadata Enable is turned on, AIBridge sends AI-detected object metadata to Cortrol VMS. In environments with a lot of detected objects, this can affect performance.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;\"><strong>Note.</strong> If you're a Cortrol Global user and registered the device using Cortrol Recording, select <strong>Use Recording Server</strong> and enter its ID and password. This option isn't needed for Cortrol Premier.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.2 AIBridge Channel Mapping</h3>\n<p>Configure the relationship between AIBridge channels and Cortrol VMS channels. Click the <strong>Mapping</strong> button to open the settings popup, and enter the recording identifier (UUID) of each channel registered in Cortrol VMS into AIBridge.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n<tr><th>AIBridge Channel</th><th>Cortrol Recording UUID</th><th>Status</th></tr>\n<tr><td>CH 1</td><td><input value=\"a1e2c9f0-3b4d-4e5f-8a1b-9c0d1e2f3a4b\" disabled style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:11px;width:100%;\"></td><td style=\"color:var(--green);\">&#9679; Connected</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CH 2</td><td><input disabled style=\"width:100%;\"></td><td style=\"color:var(--text-muted);\">Disconnected</td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n<figcaption>The recording identifier (UUID) can be found in the channel's Details menu in Cortrol Management Console</figcaption>\n</div>\n<p>Enter each UUID, then click <strong>Cameras Update</strong> to confirm they were entered correctly. Successfully connected channels show a green <strong>Connected</strong> label.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.3 Creating a Cortrol External Service</h3>\n<p>On AIBridge's <strong>Server Settings</strong> page, click <strong>Create</strong> to generate an external service.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--border);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">&#8251; Clicking Create resets the group mapping, so it will need to be mapped again. Rule settings and other configuration are not reset.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Next, create the External Service in Cortrol Management Console. Name it <strong>AI Bridge</strong>, and assign AIBridge to the External Service Group.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">&#8251; If you're using a Cortrol Recording Server, select it under server settings.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">&#8251; To use the external service, enable external use in each individual channel's configuration &ndash; this must be configured per channel.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.4 Event Action Message Settings</h3>\n<p>Event action message settings let you configure the format of the message AIBridge sends to Cortrol when an event occurs &ndash; for example, adding LPR information or counting data to the message so it's visible in Cortrol.</p>\n<p>Two content types are available: <strong>Text</strong> and <strong>Key-Value</strong>. Firmware versions before 13907 have no content-type option and operate in Text mode only. Text mode isn't recommended for Cortrol compatibility, so this guide covers the Key-Value method &ndash; upgrade to firmware 13907 or later to use it.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:520px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:110px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Content Type</span><select disabled><option>Key-Value</option><option>Text</option></select>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"section-label\">Key-Value Pairs</div>\n  <div style=\"background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;padding:10px;font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;\">\n    Plate &rarr; {{LPR NUMBER}}<br>Confidence &rarr; {{LPR CONFIDENCE}}\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"margin-top:8px;\"><span class=\"btn small primary\">Set as Default</span></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Select a string composition, then click Set as Default to build the event action message</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">&#8251; Keys and values are displayed as shown below on the Live screen. If a value is empty, its key isn't shown either.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">&#8251; Cortrol has a multi-language display issue, so characters may appear garbled.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">&#8251; Keys you enter appear as columns when searching in Cortrol.</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>Click <strong>OK</strong> to save the Cortrol action settings. If a device is registered in the External Service tab of Cortrol Management Console in the form <code>AIBridge-MacAddress</code>, the setup is correct.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.5 Creating Cortrol Events and Rules</h3>\n<p>Configure the event, action, and rule that will deliver the notification. To add a new event, click <strong>New Event</strong>, then set the event type to <strong>External Event &ndash; External Service</strong>.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">&#8251; The Target Event section shows events currently in use by AI Bridge. To receive alarms for every event, select <strong>Event</strong>.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Combine the created event type with an action to create a rule.</p>\n\n<h2>3. Demo</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.1 Live</h3>\n<p>Configure Cortrol Client to display metadata and alarms to confirm the AIBridge integration is working correctly. Clicking the bell icon at the bottom of the video shows a real-time event log on the Live screen.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">&#8251; In the event action message, entered keys are shown along with their values. A key with no value is not shown.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.2 Search</h3>\n<p>Event Search is available from Cortrol Client. In the event action message, entered keys become columns, with their corresponding values shown in that column. You can use a keyword to search for an LPR plate or an attribute.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">&#8251; A partial plate match is enough to find a result, and case is not sensitive.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">&#8251; Keyword matches against the Value, not the Key.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>4. FAQ</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">4.1 Object Metadata Transmission Option</h3>\n<p>If this feature is turned off, neither ONVIF metadata nor the metadata configured in the plugin is transmitted &ndash; this applies to metadata behavior as a whole.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">4.2 Client-Side Video Analytics Overlay Setting in Cortrol</h3>\n<p>If Video Analytics is not enabled in the Edit settings of the Cortrol Client application, metadata may not display correctly. The default value is ON &ndash; don't turn this feature off.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">4.3 Verifying the Connection Between AI Bridge and Cortrol</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>On the AI Bridge web page, click <strong>Event Rule Map</strong> under Video.</li>\n<li>Select the <strong>Action Preset</strong>, then click the previously configured Cortrol plugin's settings button.</li>\n<li>Confirm a green <strong>Connected</strong> label is shown for the Cortrol server, then click <strong>Test</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--border);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">&#8251; Before clicking Test, confirm the Cortrol server shows the green Connected status. If it shows gray Disconnected, check the server settings.</p>\n</div>\n<p>After clicking Test, a success popup appears once the message is sent successfully. Then go to Cortrol to check the alarm message.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">4.4 Displaying Object IDs in GANZ Cortrol VMS</h3>\n<p>To display the ID of each channel or object in GANZ Cortrol VMS, enable the corresponding option:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>In the GANZ Cortrol VMS Console app, click the button in the top-right corner and select <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Show object IDs</strong>, then click <strong>OK</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Once applied correctly, IDs are visible on every object &ndash; Devices, Servers, Channels, and so on.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">4.5 No Video from AIBridge in the Ganz CORTROL Client</h3>\n<p>If AIBridge is registered in Ganz CORTROL but no video appears or an error occurs, check the following in order:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Confirm the network connection with a ping test.</strong> From the Device settings menu, click <strong>Ping device</strong> to confirm the signal reaches AIBridge correctly from the CORTROL server. If the ping fails, check the network firewall settings or re-verify the IP address entered for AIBridge.</li>\n<li><strong>Check the video connection status.</strong> If the ping test passes, check the connection status inside CORTROL &ndash; in Management Console's Monitoring tab, click Channels to see the current channel status.</li>\n<li><strong>Compare the RTSP port number (default 5554).</strong> If a connection error shows up in the step above, the AIBridge RTSP port has likely been changed.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">&#8251; AIBridge's default RTSP port is 5554. Ganz CORTROL internally fixes the RTSP port to 5554 when registering AIBridge, so changing this port in the AIBridge device settings may prevent CORTROL from loading video. Set the port back to 5554 in AIBridge's settings and confirm video appears.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>5. Revision History</h2>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>v1.00 &ndash; Initial document.</li>\n<li>v1.10 &ndash; Updated captured images, added FAQ.</li>\n<li>v1.20 &ndash; Added images and supplemented content in Section 2, Configuration.</li>\n<li>v1.30 &ndash; Added content and updated images in Section 2.1, AIBridge Configuration.</li>\n<li>v1.40 &ndash; Updated the Event Action Message feature.</li>\n<li>v1.50 &ndash; Added FAQ 4.4.</li>\n<li>v1.60 &ndash; Added FAQ 4.5.</li>\n</ul>";
